.TH KOBAS 1 2000-1月 "kobas.gsea" "kobas.gsea"
.SH NAME
kobas.gsea \- Run the KOBAS style GSEA analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkobas.gsea(\fBexpr\fR as any, 
\fBcls\fR as any, 
\fBgmt\fR as any, 
\fBmethod\fR as string = "snr", 
\fBweight\fR as double = 1, 
\fBpermutations\fR as integer = 1000, 
\fBmin_size\fR as integer = 15, 
\fBmax_size\fR as integer = 500, 
\fBseed\fR as integer = 20261026, 
\fBkeep_running_sum\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBverbose\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run the KOBAS style GSEA analysis
 
 Gene Set Enrichment Analysis with the KOBAS ranking and permutation scheme: the
 genes are ranked by the signal-to-noise ratio or the t statistics between the
 two phenotype groups, then a weighted Kolmogorov-Smirnov like running sum is
 evaluated for each gene set. The significance of the enrichment score is
 estimated by permuting the phenotype class labels.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBexpr\fB \fR\- 
 the expression matrix, rows are genes and columns are samples. The value could be
 a matrix object, a \fBdataframe\fR object (rows are genes and columns are samples),
 or a file path of the \fBgct\fR / KOBAS plain text expression matrix.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcls\fB \fR\- 
 the phenotype class labels: could be a \fBphenotype\fR object, a \fBCLS\fR file path,
 an integer vector (\fB0\fR for the first phenotype group and \fB1\fR for the second
 group), or a character vector with exactly two distinct class labels.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgmt\fB \fR\- 
 the gene set collection: a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model or a GMT file path.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmethod\fB \fR\- 
 the gene ranking method: \fBsnr\fR (signal to noise ratio, default) or \fBttest\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBweight\fB \fR\- 
 the weight of the enrichment score, \fB0\fR for the unweighted Kolmogorov-Smirnov
 statistic, \fB1\fR (default) for the classic GSEA weighting and \fB2\fR for the
 over-weighted score. Any other positive value \fBp\fR will use \fB|rank|^p\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpermutations\fB \fR\- 
 the number of the phenotype label permutations, default \fB1000\fR. Set to \fB0\fR for
 skipping the significance estimation (then the \fBpvalue\fR and \fBFDR\fR columns of
 the result table will be \fBNA\fR and \fBNES\fR equals to \fBES\fR).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_size\fB \fR\- the minimum number of the mapped members of a gene set, default \fB15\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_size\fB \fR\- the maximum number of the mapped members of a gene set, default \fB500\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBseed\fB \fR\- the random seed of the permutation, default \fB20261026\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBkeep_running_sum\fB \fR\- 
 keeps the running sum of each gene set in the result objects? Default \fBFALSE\fR
 because the running sum occupies a lot of memory for large gene set collections.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBverbose\fB \fR\- prints the progress message? Default \fBTRUE\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a \fBdataframe\fR with the gene set id as the row names and the columns:
 \fBname\fR, \fBdescription\fR, \fBsize\fR, \fBES\fR, \fBNES\fR, \fBpvalue\fR, \fBFDR\fR,
 \fBes_index\fR, \fBleading_edge\fR (the hit genes before/after the enrichment score
 position, joined by \fB;\fR) and \fBhit_genes\fR.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
A positive ES means that the gene set is enriched in the first phenotype group
 (the samples labeled with \fB0\fR) because the KOBAS ranking score is
 \fBmean(group0) - mean(group1)\fR.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
KOBAS
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
